# Local build artifact — the binary is built via goreleaser/release flow, never committed
/tether

# Local out-of-band maintenance script — NOT part of tether and must never become a release
# artifact. docs/testing-standards.md §S2 records why: it defaults to 0.0.0.0, an EMPTY token
# (empty == no auth), no TTL, and plaintext TCP to an interactive root PTY — a complete remote
# code execution surface. Two successive external reviews have had to find it in a staged tree
# and block on it; ignoring that file is what stops a third from having to.
#
# If it is ever to ship, it needs fail-closed defaults (loopback bind, non-empty credential,
# finite TTL), separate agent/operator authority, and transport confidentiality — and then it
# belongs in its own increment with its own review, not carried along by an unrelated batch.
/tools/rescue.py
